# calc_gnd_bounce.py  CALCULATION (T-073, C2-005; T-092 no sockets) on hardware/frutamidi.kicad_pcb (KiCad 10.0.4)
# series elements (ASSUMPTION): castellation 0.5-1.5 nH + butted module pin 2.9-4.9 nH = 3.4-6.4 nH (V1.2: 3-10 nH socket + header)
GND path lengths (MEASUREMENT, design file): J2 pad 1 (GND terminal) -> Pico pin 23 21.99 mm; module GND pin -> Pico pin 23 30.90 mm; shared section from node (27.00,45.60) to pin 23 3.84 mm
Arc entry: E pad -> edge track (y = 68.00) -> J2 pad 1: up to 65.2 mm (E11); this section and the trunk to the node are common to module and Pico (whole-board rise, no differential at IC pins)

IEC 61000-4-2 4 kV contact (SOURCE EE-S16 from memory, upper tolerance): Ipk 17.2 A, tr 0.6-1.0 ns, I(30 ns) 8 A
case (ASSUMPTION)                   L_diff nH di/dt A/ns  Vb peak V   I2C peak A     I2C Q nC
0.7 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 0.6 ns            6.1       23.0        140         0.63         0.38
0.7 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 1.0 ns            6.1       13.8         84         0.38         0.38
0.7 nH/mm, pin 6 nH, tr 0.6 ns            9.1       23.0        209         0.94         0.57
0.7 nH/mm, pin 6 nH, tr 1.0 ns            9.1       13.8        125         0.56         0.56
1.0 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 0.6 ns            7.2       23.0        167         0.75         0.45
1.0 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 1.0 ns            7.2       13.8        100         0.45         0.45
1.0 nH/mm, pin 6 nH, tr 0.6 ns           10.2       23.0        236         1.06         0.64
1.0 nH/mm, pin 6 nH, tr 1.0 ns           10.2       13.8        141         0.64         0.64

Worst case: module GND - Pico GND bounce 236 V for ~1 ns; after the first peak (slope to I(30 ns)) 3.2 V
  through R15/R16 (220 ohm, then the BSS138 level shifters on the module): <= 1.06 A, <= 0.64 nC per line
  RP2040 HBM 4 kV (SOURCE EE-S28, stated for digital FT pins only) = 2.67 A peak, 400 nC -> injected charge 0.2 % of the HBM charge, peak 0.40x the HBM peak
  NOT CONFIRMED: GP26/GP27 (I2C1 on the PCB) are ADC-capable pins; the extracted RP2040 table gives HBM 4 kV for FT pins and CDM 500 V, no separate HBM value for these pins was found (EE-S28)
  without the arc (strike through Rx into the MPR121 pin): pin current 1.10 A (R 3k3 + 330 ohm source, CALCULATION), bounce scaled by 0.06 -> 15 V
DECISION INPUT: the 1.40 mm gap acts as a spark gap to GND at every terminal; it keeps the strike off the MPR121 pin; residual risk = 236 V / ~1 ns GND bounce between module and Pico (ASSUMPTION-based), not measured
